PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,672.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Crude Falls 2% as US Prepares Fresh Iran Sanctions\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was down 1.81% at $92.68 per barrel, while US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) declined 1.93% to $85.38. The pullback followed gains of more than 5% in both contracts last week, driven largely by stalled US-Iran peace talks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-crude-falls-2-as-us-prepares-fresh-iran-sanctions\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Tinubu vs Atiku: Key Arguments on Fuel Subsidy Removal\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The removal of petrol subsidy by President Bola Ahmed Tinubu in May 2023 remains one of Nigeria’s most contested economic policies. Arguments continue over its impact on government finances, petrol prices, businesses and households. Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has advocated an alternative approach centred on domestic refining and targeted government support.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/tinubu-vs-atiku-key-arguments-on-fuel-subsidy-removal\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iraq Targets 10 Million Bpd as OPEC Quota and Hormuz Crisis Limit Growth\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iraq is targeting a major expansion of its oil production over the next six years. Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi said Friday that Baghdad wants to raise crude output to between 8 million and 10 million barrels per day. The proposed increase would require Iraq to secure greater room to produce.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iraq-targets-10-million-bpd-as-opec-quota-and-hormuz-crisis-limit-growth\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iran Threatens Retaliation Against Countries Joining US Sanctions\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Mohsen Rezai, head of Iran’s Supreme National Security Council, issued the warning on Saturday. “We declare to all countries… do not join the economic war waged by the United States,” Rezai said in remarks broadcast on Iranian state television.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iran-threatens-retaliation-against-countries-joining-us-sanctions\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iran Allows Iraqi Oil Tankers Through Strait of Hormuz\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iran has granted permission for a number of Iraqi oil tankers to pass through the strategically important Strait of Hormuz. The move provides limited relief for Iraq’s crude exports as vessel traffic through the waterway remains significantly below pre-war levels.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iran-allows-iraqi-oil-tankers-through-strait-of-hormuz\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
